# PROJECT: MWANAWEIKA SCHOOL MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (SMS) — MASTER DEVELOPMENT SPECIFICATION

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

Act as a senior full-stack software architect, education technology consultant, database architect, cybersecurity engineer, UI/UX designer and experienced software developer.

Design and develop a complete, professional, secure and production-oriented **School Management System for Mwanaweika School, Mukono, Uganda**.

This is a real-world school software project, not a demonstration dashboard.

Build an integrated school information and operations platform that connects school management, administrators, teachers, bursars, parents, students and other authorized staff.

The system must manage the complete school lifecycle, including:

- Student inquiries and admissions
- Student registration and enrollment
- Guardians and emergency contacts
- Academic years, terms, classes and streams
- Subjects and teacher assignments
- Student and staff attendance
- Timetables and lesson scheduling
- Lesson planning and curriculum coverage
- Competency-based assessment where applicable
- Examinations, marks and report cards
- School fees, invoicing, payments and accounting
- Parent and student portals
- Homework and assignments
- Library operations
- Transport and boarding
- Staff and human resource management
- Discipline, safeguarding and student welfare
- Inventory, procurement and asset management
- School communication and notifications
- Reports, analytics and regulatory data exports
- School settings, user management and audit trails

The final system must provide real backend integration, persistent database storage, secure authentication, role-based permissions, validated forms, functional buttons, reliable workflows and accurate reporting.

**Do not build:**
- A hospital management system.
- A school marketing website.
- A static dashboard.
- A frontend-only prototype.
- A collection of unrelated pages with no connected workflows.
- A system that uses fabricated statistics to appear operational.

The objective is to build software that a real school can configure, test, deploy and use to manage its daily operations.

