## 37. SECURITY, PRIVACY AND DATA PROTECTION

Student information is confidential.

Design the system with Uganda's Data Protection and Privacy Act, 2019, applicable regulations and relevant education-sector requirements in mind.

The school must obtain appropriate professional compliance review before using real student data.

### Security requirements

- Role-based access control
- Backend permission enforcement
- Secure authentication
- Strong password hashing
- HTTPS in production
- Secure session management
- Input validation
- SQL injection protection
- Cross-site scripting protection
- CSRF protection where applicable
- Rate limiting
- Secure file uploads
- Restricted document access
- Audit logging
- Database backups
- Secure environment variables
- Access revocation
- Session timeout
- Account activity monitoring

### Privacy requirements

- Collect only necessary personal information.
- Restrict sensitive student records.
- Verify guardian relationships.
- Record relevant consent and lawful processing information.
- Support guardian access revocation.
- Support correction requests for inaccurate personal data.
- Establish appropriate data retention periods.
- Restrict data exports.
- Log sensitive record access.
- Avoid exposing confidential information in application logs.
- Protect health and safeguarding records.
- Do not make religion or other sensitive personal information mandatory unless there is a lawful and necessary reason.

### Audit logging

Record:

- User
- Action
- Module
- Record affected
- Date and time
- Relevant before-and-after changes
- IP address where appropriate
- Approval details where applicable

Log sensitive record access, changes, exports, printing, financial transactions and administrative actions.

Do not allow ordinary users to edit or delete audit records.

### Backup and recovery

Document:

- Database backup schedule
- Backup retention
- Recovery procedures
- Restore testing
- Access to backup files
- Incident response
- Data breach escalation

A backup process is not complete until restoration has been tested.

